# CommAgent — Cursor/Copilot Rules

Read STATE.md first, always — it has full architecture, stack, and current
progress checklist. This file is just coding conventions.

## Non-negotiables
- Do NOT change track, architecture, or tech stack. Time is the constraint,
  not the idea. If something in the stack seems hard, find the fastest
  correct implementation — don't swap the approach.
- The self-critique step MUST remain a distinct LLM call/graph node, separate
  from the draft step. This is the project's entire differentiator — never
  collapse them to save an API call.
- Keep every function small and single-purpose. This is a time-boxed build;
  debuggability > cleverness.

## Backend (Python/FastAPI)
- Match existing code style in the file you're editing before introducing new
  patterns.
- Every external call (Notion, Telegram, Claude, Resend) goes through its own
  file in `integrations/` — never inline API calls in `agent/` or `main.py`.
- Log every agent step (retrieve/draft/critique/decide) to a place the
  frontend `/logs` endpoint can read — this trail IS the demo.
- Fail loud in dev (raise/print full errors), fail soft in the Telegram-facing
  path (never let a raw exception reach the user's chat).

## Frontend (Next.js)
- Keep the dashboard to one page: live reasoning trail, polling `/api/logs`.
  No auth, no extra pages — not worth the time.
- Plain, readable UI over polished — function over form given the deadline.

## Env vars (never hardcode)
NOTION_API_KEY, TELEGRAM_BOT_TOKEN, ANTHROPIC_API_KEY, RESEND_API_KEY (if used)

## When stuck / low on time
- Ship the happy path first (KB has the answer -> confident -> posts).
- Then the escalation path (KB doesn't have it -> not confident -> escalates).
  This second path IS the demo's money-shot — don't skip it under time
  pressure even if polish suffers elsewhere.
- Update STATE.md's "Current status" checklist as each step completes, so any
  assistant picking this up mid-build knows exactly where things stand.